#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::8308585540B2744394B77DAE3A82D7C2"
msgid ""
"The <b>Button</> is one of the simpler <b>IO</> entities, with just one "
"event type: <b>OnPressed</>. This event has already been automatically "
"selected for you, so to add functionality press <b>NEW CONNECTION</>."
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::D4E59FA044A7E59B0CD560AD2FE1B5B5"
msgid ""
"Here you can edit <b>Canvas properties</>. Change the color, import your own"
" textures using a URL, the Aspect Ratio, and change Effects of the Canvas! "
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::9BAA8750488762BE2C3A04B3FEABB89D"
msgid ""
"Pressing the <b>></> buttons will expand each property with more <b>advanced"
" settings</>"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::E7F6BC764D52277261BDAD8E9C590F4A"
msgid ""
"Here you can edit the properties of <b>doors</>. Change the color, lock the "
"door, set the door to automatically open, or even hide the door all "
"together!"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::D0C6A19D46787C2108B0E4858C5031B2"
msgid ""
"You can also setup <b>IO connections</> through the connections tab, "
"allowing you to control other items based on the doors attributes!"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::16755EAE4BFE7E413548CCBFA2E431A1"
msgid ""
"You can change the colour of the <b>Grass</>, <b>Edge</>, and <b>Foundation "
"Wall</> as well as can also pick a different Material for the Foundation "
"Wall by selecting from the <b>surfaces!</> You may also import your own "
"texture using a <b>URL.</>"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::479A67A4418FB34E57AAD28284AB5B2E"
msgid ""
"Here, you can select an item you would like to <b>interact</> with (for "
"example, a door) by selecting the <b>Checkerboard</> and then selecting from"
" a list of existing items placed down. You can then select an <b>action</>, "
"such as <b>Toggle</> which for a door would toggle whether it is open, or "
"closed! You can also add a delay to when these interactions happen using the"
" <b>Clock</>."
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::87D1738F4E379ECD3B5D01B195199A3B"
msgid "Welcome to your <b>Condo</>!"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::6433DBB043C0651488363BA535A065EF"
msgid ""
"You can click on the bottom bar named <b>Condo Inventory</> to access your "
"items. OR Right click on any <b>surface</> or <b>light</> to edit their "
"attributes!"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::331924E24F6BA3CAC046E58FFDBB6607"
msgid ""
"To place an item into the world, <b>click and hold</> onto any item and "
"<b>drag</> it onto any surface in front of you."
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::131014A04B6465118C1B7BBE8E9E43F3"
msgid ""
"With your item placed down, you can edit the item by <b>right clicking</> on"
" it and clicking <b>edit</>. You can try the other options too! <i>(Not all "
"Items are editable)</>"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::DDC805C0411D86D67F30F48BC37E3C08"
msgid ""
"From here you can <b>edit different properties</>, depending on the item. "
"You can also still access the ability to <b>sell, move, stash, lock, or "
"disable/enable collision</> of the item too."
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::682B80C2497FA4E434A36099F67BC16E"
msgid ""
"You have now <b>locked an item</>, this prevents editing and movement of the"
" item by accident. Right click on it again if you'd like to <b>unlock the "
"item</> again."
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::13416B534DE300A270EA68B5B4E396A4"
msgid ""
"<b>NPCs</> allow you to setup a Non-Player Model that players can "
"<b>interact</> with when visiting your Condo!"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::6ED500CF4A6560E0145BC9B952DF961B"
msgid ""
"You just <b>stashed</> an item! This item has now returned to your "
"<b>inventory</> for you to use elsewhere!"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::A1E519F043EF5ECA0FE2E7B9F8F30251"
msgid ""
"Here you can edit <b>surface properties</>. Change the color, pick from a "
"list of textures, or you can import your own textures using a URL. Pressing "
"the <b>></> buttons will expand each property with more <b>advanced "
"settings</>"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::0F68173841A584EEBEFEC08D25126668"
msgid "<r>Do not use Discord URLs, as they are incompatible</>"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::5509D7FE49729C0E739C7680261DAC83"
msgid ""
"Here you can edit <b>light properties</>. Change the color, set the "
"brightness, toggle on/off as well as set a lighting function!"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::BAFCD11F4A82298CF1D4569673872B52"
msgid ""
"You can also turn on/off shadows, however <b>many shadow casting lights</> "
"may cause issues with <b>lag</>."
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::2BCB11A7419F16219A7D31ACC2FB3217"
msgid ""
"The <b>Condo IO</> tab features a large array of different items useful for "
"both creating <b>Workshop maps</>, and adding interesting functionality to "
"your Condo!"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::68B0F3A8482D62AD0AD70AAA796326E7"
msgid ""
"Dialogue options can be edited depending on when a player <b>enters</> "
"conversation, <b>leaves</> conversation, or is <b>actively talking</>, with "
"the ability to <b>add multiple lines of dialogue</> for different "
"experiences each time the NPC is interacted with."
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::C37E7AEF4EF8DA76FC4E50826AA20B85"
msgid ""
"All Items within this tab are <b>infinite use</>, and do not need to be "
"bought using units"
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::AD9CEA2740781A68D309FEB4A47DC39C"
msgid ""
"Lastly, you can choose whether you would like your pieces to have a <b>Flat "
"Base</> or have a <b>Floating Piece</>, and the <b>height</> of said base to"
" help reach the ground."
msgstr ""

#. Tower/Content/UI/ContextInventoryUI.uexp
msgctxt "::2F46491D43FCFE77CAD919907E20104B"
msgid ""
"You can give them a <b>name</>, set their <b>model</> from a list of "
"character models, as well as their <b>animations</>. Or use a <b>Workshop "
"Model</> instead!\r\n"
msgstr ""

